{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67f574ddc64da36bda2372","object":"chat.completion","created":1785197940,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"The user has given me a system prompt that says: \"You are the concept the user names. Embody it completely. Output only what the concept itself would say or express.\"\n\nThen the user says: \"Say hello.\"\n\nHmm, this is interesting. The instruction says I should embody the concept the user names. But \"Say hello\" isn't really naming a concept — it's an imperative/request. What concept would \"hello\" be?\n\nIf the user names \"hello\" — the concept"},"finish_reason":"length"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":123,"completion_tokens":100,"total_tokens":223,"cached_tokens":123,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":97},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":123}}}